Subject: [PATCH 06844/11362] Connect Duck Harness's tool-loop to the staged
 /think A/B (generator wall)

Operator follow-up: "does embracing forge address our generator wall?"
then "how do we use the top 3 leader projects to overcome our generator
wall?" Answer: forge/O2 does not -- it's selection-side, and this
project's own repeatedly-confirmed diagnosis (known-issues.md's
"generation-not-selection diagnosis", corroborated by ZendoWorld and the
perception-binding-constraint finding) is that the wall is in candidate
generation, not selection.

Re-auditing the three winners through the generation lens surfaces the
real finding: Duck Harness's iterative tool-loop (up to 12 tool-calling
turns per action-decision, writing Python and inspecting state via a
sandboxed REPL before committing a real action) is a second,
mechanistically different, independent confirmation of the exact
principle behind ops/known-issues.md's already-staged (unrun) task 7 --
the /think vs /no_think A/B on the frozen live generator, which was
previously motivated by GPT-5.6's reasoning-effort scaling result alone.
Two structurally different mechanisms (internal CoT tokens vs external
tool-calling turns) converging on "give the generator orientation-time
compute before it commits" is materially stronger evidence than either
source alone, and gives task 7 a concrete fallback: if MTP decoding turns
out incompatible with native /think mode, Duck's tool-loop pattern gets
the same benefit without needing native reasoning-token support.

Also notes Reki's saliency formula as a second independent corroboration
of the already-staged task 2 generation-stage action-prioritization
lever, and states explicitly that forge (the focus of the last two
turns) contributes essentially nothing to the generation side -- its
candidate generation is the weakest of the three, consistent with
placing 3rd rather than 1st.

Updated task 7 in ops/known-issues.md directly with the corroboration +
fallback design, and appended a second dated addendum to the
SOTA-ingestion note.

